1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,840
You've saved your first €1,000.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:03,742
Now what?

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,685
Your bank offers a fund.

4
00:00:05,705 --> 00:00:07,515
A friend talks about crypto.

5
00:00:07,535 --> 00:00:09,901
Someone online has a secret strategy.

6
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:13,132
So you do nothing, and the money just sits there,

7
00:00:13,152 --> 00:00:15,524
losing a little to inflation every year.

8
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:18,156
And here's the part nobody tells you.

9
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,405
Your first €1,000 isn't about getting rich.

10
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:24,409
It's about building the habit that will.

11
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,990
Here are the eight steps, in order.

12
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:27,919
Let's begin.

13
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:29,344
One.

14
00:00:29,364 --> 00:00:31,133
Kill expensive debt first.

15
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:35,537
If you have a credit card or a loan at 15 or 20% a year,

16
00:00:35,557 --> 00:00:36,866
pay that off first.

17
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:38,808
Every euro of that debt you

18
00:00:38,828 --> 00:00:40,718
repay earns you that rate, guaranteed.

19
00:00:40,738 --> 00:00:42,812
No investment promises that.

20
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:44,330
Two.

21
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:46,068
Keep a small safety cushion.

22
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:49,583
Before investing, keep some cash for surprises:

23
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:52,211
a broken phone, a car repair, a big bill.

24
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:54,468
Start with one month of expenses,

25
00:00:54,488 --> 00:00:56,533
and build towards three to six.

26
00:00:56,553 --> 00:00:58,784
Otherwise, the first emergency forces you

27
00:00:58,804 --> 00:01:00,526
to sell at the worst moment.

28
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:01,923
Three.

29
00:01:01,943 --> 00:01:03,249
Use the right account.

30
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:07,223
Many European countries have accounts with tax advantages.

31
00:01:07,243 --> 00:01:08,798
The PEA in France.

32
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,248
The ISA in the UK.

33
00:01:10,268 --> 00:01:11,852
The ISK in Sweden.

34
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,610
The same investment, inside the right account,

35
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:17,295
can leave you with noticeably more after tax.

36
00:01:17,315 --> 00:01:19,117
Check what your country offers.

37
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:20,496
Four.

38
00:01:20,516 --> 00:01:22,653
Pick a regulated, low-cost broker.

39
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:25,141
Look for a broker regulated

40
00:01:25,161 --> 00:01:26,642
in the EU or the UK.

41
00:01:26,662 --> 00:01:30,472
In the EU, if a broker fails and can't give your investments back,

42
00:01:30,492 --> 00:01:34,046
compensation schemes cover at least €20,000.

43
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,630
Then look at the fees:

44
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:38,490
per order, per year, and for currency exchange.

45
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:42,081
On €1,000, a €10 fee is already 1%.

46
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:43,611
Five.

47
00:01:43,631 --> 00:01:45,069
Buy the whole market.

48
00:01:45,767 --> 00:01:48,572
Instead of guessing which company will win, buy them all,

49
00:01:48,592 --> 00:01:50,734
with one global index ETF.

50
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:55,242
One fund can hold well over a thousand companies across dozens of countries,

51
00:01:55,262 --> 00:01:58,422
for around 0.2% a year or less.

52
00:01:58,442 --> 00:02:00,896
In Europe, look for UCITS in the name.

53
00:02:02,033 --> 00:02:02,338
Six.

54
00:02:02,358 --> 00:02:03,381
Automate it.

55
00:02:04,233 --> 00:02:07,003
Many brokers let you set up a monthly savings plan,

56
00:02:07,023 --> 00:02:08,463
sometimes for free.

57
00:02:08,483 --> 00:02:10,328
Even €50 a month.

58
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:13,908
Your first €1,000 becomes the start of a habit,

59
00:02:13,928 --> 00:02:15,177
not a one-off bet.

60
00:02:16,033 --> 00:02:18,830
€1,000 left alone for thirty years at

61
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:23,148
7% a year grows to about €7,600.

62
00:02:23,168 --> 00:02:27,583
Add €100 a month, and it's about €130,000.

63
00:02:28,667 --> 00:02:29,000
Seven.

64
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,248
Then don't touch it.

65
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,427
In early 2020,

66
00:02:32,447 --> 00:02:33,886
stock markets fell about a

67
00:02:33,906 --> 00:02:35,077
third in a few weeks.

68
00:02:35,097 --> 00:02:37,137
People who sold locked in the loss.

69
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,694
The S&P 500 was back at its

70
00:02:39,714 --> 00:02:42,135
record about five months after the bottom.

71
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:44,203
Don't check it every day.

72
00:02:44,223 --> 00:02:45,768
Once a month is plenty.

73
00:02:45,788 --> 00:02:47,082
Once a year is better.

74
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:48,636
Eight.

75
00:02:48,656 --> 00:02:49,950
Keep learning, slowly.

76
00:02:50,767 --> 00:02:51,877
Read one good book.

77
00:02:51,897 --> 00:02:53,087
Watch the fees.

78
00:02:53,107 --> 00:02:56,287
Ignore anyone promising fast, guaranteed returns.

79
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,245
If it sounds too good to be true,

80
00:02:58,265 --> 00:02:59,276
it usually is.

81
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:01,679
Final message.

82
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,213
The best first investment isn't a stock.

83
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:06,448
It's a system:

84
00:03:06,468 --> 00:03:09,163
no expensive debt, a cushion, the right account,

85
00:03:09,183 --> 00:03:11,923
one cheap global fund, and automatic deposits.

86
00:03:12,633 --> 00:03:13,029
Boring?

87
00:03:13,049 --> 00:03:13,279
Yes.

88
00:03:13,299 --> 00:03:14,998
That's exactly why it works.

89
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:18,255
This is education, not financial advice.

90
00:03:18,275 --> 00:03:20,895
Rules differ by country, so check yours.

91
00:03:20,915 --> 00:03:22,550
If this helped, subscribe.

92
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:22,800
Next up:

93
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:26,648
compound interest, explained so simply it feels illegal.
